#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/et.rc -- Estonian (Estonia), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "et"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. Left to right, Latin script with the letters õ ä ö ü (õ is the
// Estonian letter, not the Finnish one) and š ž. The tone is the one of Windows in Estonian: the
// text of an instruction and of a question addresses the reader politely in the plural (te:
// "Valige", "Klõpsake", "Kas soovite"), the names of buttons and menu items are the imperative of
// the singular ("Ava", "Salvesta"); Estonian has no grammatical gender, so the voice of the
// author and of the reader need none (RULES 14). Quotes are the Estonian „…“. No case ending is
// put on a substitution ({0}, {1}): the phrase is built so that the word before it carries the
// case ("klahvita {1}", "versioon {0}"). The key names stay in Latin letters, as the hotkey field
// prints them (RULES 4). The name of the program is not translated and is not inflected.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Estonian — `[general] language = "et"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
